\section{Related work}
\label{sec:related}

\paragraph{Regression estimators of the global effect.}
\citet{chin2019regression} proposed the estimator we study: build covariates from functions of the assignment vector, fit the outcome on them, predict at global treatment and global control, and difference. It rests on an exogeneity (correct response model) assumption and uses resampling for inference. \citet{chin2019regression} also observes that the exposure covariates under global treatment and control lie away from their observed distribution, and relates this to off-policy evaluation, qualitatively and with one example. \citet{han2023model} generate and select graph-based and treatment-based covariates and give block-bootstrap intervals, with semi-synthetic and real checks. We take both as the estimator family. We do not claim the extrapolation viewpoint as new; what we add is a quantified split of the error, tested across mechanisms, graphs and designs, together with a map of where the estimator loses, and a diagnostic computed from the experiment.

\paragraph{Exposure-mapping estimators.}
Horvitz--Thompson and H\'ajek estimators with a specified exposure mapping \citep{aronow2017estimating,eckles2017design}, usually paired with graph-cluster randomization \citep{ugander2013graph,karrer2021network}, are the design-based baselines. \citet{thiyageswaran2024data} choose the exposure threshold from the data; \citet{shirani2024causal} fit a message-passing model. \citet{gao2023causal} study regression fits whose estimands are contrasts between exposure conditions, with design-based guarantees; the global effect, and the extrapolation it needs, is a different target.

\paragraph{Misspecified or unknown interference.}
Difference in means is consistent for a marginalised estimand under unknown interference \citep{savje2021average}; misspecified exposure mappings separate the estimand from the assumption \citep{leung2022causal,savje2023causal}; \citet{yu2022estimating} estimate the total effect without the network. Our setting fixes the estimand to the global effect and lets the response model be wrong.

\paragraph{Designs.}
Cluster-based, correlated and staggered-rollout designs \citep{ugander2013graph,ugander2023randomized,candogan2023correlated,cortez2022staggered,chen2023optimized} change the distribution of exposures the regression sees; we cross the estimator with Bernoulli and graph-cluster assignment. The analogy to limited overlap \citep{crump2009dealing,damour2021overlap} is the source of our extrapolation framing.
EOF
